From b225d8f47518864c6dcffc604fa81e053d7ca33e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuta Saito <yuta@goodnotes.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:05:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [cmake] Allow opting out of the CMP0157 Swift
 split-compilation model

CMake's Swift split-compilation model (policy CMP0157 NEW) drives swiftc with
an output-file-map that only names 'object' outputs. When the compiler is asked
for LTO ('-lto=llvm-full' / '-lto=llvm-thin') the driver emits LLVM bitcode
instead and derives '<basename>.bc' names in the working directory, so the
object files CMake declared are never produced and the static-library step
fails with 'error opening input file ... .swift.obj'.

Let a build that needs bitcode libraries set
FOUNDATION_DISABLE_SWIFT_SPLIT_COMPILATION to keep the one-step
compile-and-archive model, where the driver names its own outputs and archives
them itself. The default is unchanged.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 402d32b5..351272ec 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -21,8 +21,17 @@ if(POLICY CMP0156)
     cmake_policy(SET CMP0156 NEW)
 endif()
 
-if(POLICY CMP0157)
+if(POLICY CMP0157 AND NOT FOUNDATION_DISABLE_SWIFT_SPLIT_COMPILATION)
     # New Swift build model: improved incremental build performance and LSP support
+    #
+    # The split-compilation model drives swiftc with an output-file-map that only
+    # names 'object' outputs. When the Swift compiler is asked for LTO
+    # ('-lto=llvm-full'/'-lto=llvm-thin') the driver produces LLVM bitcode
+    # instead and derives '<basename>.bc' names in the working directory, so the
+    # object files CMake expects are never created and the archive step fails.
+    # Builds that need bitcode libraries set
+    # FOUNDATION_DISABLE_SWIFT_SPLIT_COMPILATION to fall back to the one-step
+    # compile-and-archive model, which lets the driver name its own outputs.
     cmake_policy(SET CMP0157 NEW)
 endif()
 
